  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "Honest, self-critical, provisional \u2014 acknowledges weaknesses and risks of the mapping",
    "Q1_identity": "An isomorphism record testing the structural mapping between physical coherence (Shannon entropy, quantum coherence) and theological divine order",
    "Q2_domain": "Physics/Information Theory \u2194 Christian Theology",
    "Q3_claim": "Coherence (as anti-entropy, structured order) is structurally isomorphic to divine order (harmony, wisdom, peace) in the topology of order-from-input, degradation-in-isolation, and signal-over-noise",
    "Q4_support": "Shannon entropy formalism, quantum decoherence, biblical texts (Genesis, Proverbs, 1 Cor, Colossians, John), Penrose's Weyl curvature hypothesis",
    "Q5_dependencies": "ISO-001 (Trinity), ISO-003 (Entropy/Sin), ISO-006 (Information), ISO-009 (Compression), ISO-011 (Superposition); axioms A3.1, A3.2, D3.1, P3.1, P3.2",
    "Q6_consequences": "If valid, it constrains theology: process theology's God-as-chaos is structurally incoherent; divine action should produce order; creation is inherently coherence-increasing. If invalid, it warns against equivocation in the framework.",
    "Q7_kill": "Show divine action is as likely to produce noise as signal; show 'coherence' does no independent physical work; define an independent measure of divine harmony that diverges from physical coherence on specific test cases"
  },
